# Trivy suppression list for go-enclave.
#
# INTENTIONALLY EMPTY. Nothing is suppressed and nothing should be without a
# reason recorded in place: one CVE id per line, each with a
# comment naming why it does not apply here and what would make it apply again.
#
# The file itself is required. Both the nightly Trivy job (nightly.yml, whose
# note says each repo supplies its own) and `make trivy` pass
# `--ignorefile .trivyignore`, and trivy treats a missing ignore file as a FATAL
# flag error rather than as an empty list — which is what reddened the nightly
# on main while `make security` stayed green locally.
#
# Format: https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/
